## Agent Roles

Each specialist agent reads its task from `bd show <id>`.

| Agent | Role |
|---|---|
| `@backend-dev` | Implements Python code for the claimed task |
| `@qa-engineer` | Writes tests (TDD red phase) for the claimed task |
| `@lancedb-specialist` | LanceDB schema, queries, FTS, sync patterns |
| `@tech-lead` | Creates/refines `bd` tasks from requirements |
| `@reviewer` | Reviews completed work via `superpowers:requesting-code-review` |
| `@orchestrator` | Coordinates multi-agent parallel work via `bd ready --json` |

---

## Anti-Patterns — Never Do These

- Skip brainstorming and "just code it"
- Write production code before a failing test
- Claim "done" without running the verification command
- Start work without claiming a `bd` task first
- Make multiple unrelated fixes in one commit
- Trust a sub-agent's report without running verification yourself
- Use any markdown file to track task progress — `bd` is the only tracker

