## Specialist Templates (on-demand)

When no existing agent covers the need, use [claude-code-templates](https://github.com/davila7/claude-code-templates) as a **reference library**.

The templates are written for Claude Code (they output to `.claude/agents/`), so they don't install directly into Cursor. Instead:

1. Browse available templates:
   ```powershell
   npx claude-code-templates@latest
   ```
2. Download the one you need:
   ```powershell
   npx claude-code-templates@latest --agent mcp-dev-team/mcp-server-architect --yes
   ```
3. The generated file lands in `.claude/agents/<name>.md`. Copy its instructions into a new file under `.cursor/agents/<name>.md`, adding the Cursor frontmatter:
   ```
   ---
   name: <agent-name>
   model: inherit
   description: <one-line description>
   ---
   ```

Categories most relevant to this project: `mcp-dev-team`, `python-architect`, `security`, `database`.
